"body":"A camera plate is retained by a passive rotary toe and a separate rear lip. This task requires physical release, edge clearance and a supported transfer to a receiving pad, representing camera/sensor servicing. The task folder includes the native scene, numerical endpoint scorer, robot-only reference controller, exact layout/material inventory, pinned installation instructions and licensed camera appearance.\n\nThe closest new board neighbor, TK-NCPNT9, measures registration and over-centre clamping of a loose workpiece against a compliant backstop. This task starts with a captured plate and measures rotary-toe release followed by clearing an independent rear retaining lip and supported dismounting. Other nearby camera-assembly, DIN-rail and latch-release families are disclosed in the README.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Three native scripted demonstrations reached 1.0 in 643 controls (32.15 simulated seconds), including the registered Inspect Robots scorer.\n- Exactly one hosted Dream-1 trial scored 0.0 at the 2,400-control limit (120 seconds). Gateway-session retries and standard joint-target clipping are documented; no repeat trial was made.\n- A gentle direct-lift control scored 0.0 with the cam engaged. A deliberate drop permanently scored 0.0 despite later upright pad placement.\n- Nine scorer tests, all five offline reachability plans and three USD structural checks pass. Runtime, seeds and executable fingerprints are included.\n\nThe fixture is a nominal rigid mechanism, not a manufacturer replica or a material-damage model. No real-hardware trial is claimed. Media M-PRZQHX contains the actual Dream-1 video, full-score scripted demo and matching initial setup screenshot.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:13:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T04:16:13Z","closed_at":"2026-11-12T04:16:13Z","merged_at":"2026-11-12T04:16:12Z","merge_commit_sha":"0c8245f915e54fa4467bea382058c3075edbb17c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],